It'd been about two years since I last played Nethack, but I finally
had the urge to play again (at least for a little while) so I got hold
of 3.4.3 and went for one of the easier classes. I almost went for a
Wizard, but after so long and given how much I seemed to have
forgotten I thought a Valkyrie was more realistic. :-) I was still
expecting several YASDs, but somehow - and with a decent slice of luck
it has to be said - I made it first time.

However, I did have serious trouble with my AC when I first got to the
castle, about -7 or so I think it was. I didn't have reflection
either. I remember having to go all the way back to the mines to get
some undamaged armour (as well as getting the candles I'd missed),
which was all a bit tedious, but I was rather happier about this when
I cleared out the town's wand shop (by buying the two of the four
wands I hadn't bought or identified already) - the expensive one was a
wand of wishing. Nice. :-) I got GDSM and saved the other wishes for
later. At some point I'd also picked up reflection and genocided MFs,
MMFs and `L', so in the end the castle wasn't a problem. And it turned
out both the wands of wishing had been 0:3, so for once I was never
short of wishes. I even tried to avoid using them, to some extent.

One of the more stupid things I did was reading unidentified scrolls
once I knew they weren't cursed. I only did this a few times, and
admittedly it did lead to my identifying genocide a lot earlier than
I'd otherwise have done (identify scrolls were downright rare until
Gehennom), but it also meant I had some rather annoying amnesia to
deal with.

Another annoying mistake was dropping about 25000 gold in the Sanctum
when I got burdened while picking up a cockatrice corpse - not a bad
idea in itself, but I forgot to pick up the gold again, and didn't
remember until I'd reached the Valley and couldn't be bothered to go
back for it. So my intrinsic AC wasn't so great, I think I only
managed 6 points of protection in all.

The planes were mostly ok. On Fire, I got the message "r - an uncursed
scroll of gold detection. It burns to a crisp." and had to check the
inventory to make sure this wasn't a new feature. :-) Unfortunately on
Water I screwed up by reading my last ?oGD stunned instead of
confused, and under the circumstances ended up wishing for another.
Rather frustrating, if only I'd had a blank scroll I wouldn't have
needed that wish. Though on *Water*, I suppose I could have dipped a
scroll easily enough...? Or I could have just used the Orb instead. Oh
well.

I remembered reading (probably here) that Mjollnir is a bit weak on
Astral, so I mostly switched to Fire Brand there. It did seem to cut
through the crowd a bit better. Just as well, as I ended up visiting
all three altars:



